#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""decdn-compose: set up and operate this directory's Compose project.

A thin wrapper around `docker compose`: every service command it runs is plain
`docker compose` against compose.yaml (plus compose.override.yaml when present,
which a bare `-f compose.yaml` would silently drop). It adds what Compose cannot
do on its own:

  init      the host side of each profile: system accounts, directories, .env
            with the real uids, the env-file templates, and every secret that is
            generated on the host (node keys, keystore password, API token)
  check     a preflight (also run by `up`): files, owners, modes, settings, the
            node's config against the decdn CLI, and ports held by something else
  up / stop / restart / down
            refuse while sponsord holds an unconfirmed pool top-up, which a stop
            or a recreate would forget (README.md, "Operate")
  health    probe each running service
  cli       the decdn CLI from the node image (no host install needed)
  backup    an age-encrypted archive of the active profiles' keys and secrets

Python 3.11+, standard library only. Run it as root (sudo): Compose reads the
root-only env files whenever it creates a container. It never prints a secret
and never overwrites one.
"""

